    "Pentazocine mean F (~18%) is close to the 20% threshold, and some individual/L2 values exceed it, adding uncertainty.",
    "L2 outlier values (pentazocine ~20–30%, estradiol 30–40%) are nonvoting and conflict with more direct measurements."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L2 records reinforce the L1 low-F evidence: quantitative values for tetrabenazine (0.1–8.5%), meptazinol (~4.5–12%), pentazocine (mean ~18%), 2-methoxyestradiol (~1–3%), apocynin (2.8–8.3%), aniracetam (0.2–11.4%), curcumin (~1%), and estradiol (~1–11%) all fall below or near the 20% threshold. The query's phenol, basic N-methyl piperidine, ketone, and enol ether motifs align with these low-F scaffolds; high-F comparators are not structurally applicable. Therefore F >= 20% is not supported; prediction remains low with moderate confidence."
}

